- Single-exposure F: cluster-robust F-test of the instrument in the first
  stage (equals squared t-stat for a single instrument).
- Dual-exposure F: Sanderson-Windmeijer conditional F (cluster-robust Wald
  form), testing instrument relevance conditional on the other endogenous
  regressor.
- Endogeneity: control-function (Wooldridge robust Durbin-Wu-Hausman)
  test; p-value of the first-stage residual(s) in the outcome equation,
  cluster-robust by participant.
